WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.277
Hi, I'm Lanyard!

00:00:02.277 --> 00:00:06.225
Here's how a coding agent rewrites an optimizer while the model trains.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:12.545
The optimizer becomes code an agent keeps rewriting.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.360
One program watches the run.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.175
The other makes every update.

00:00:17.842 --> 00:00:19.950
Your training loop stays the same.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.816
At every update, the updater program turns gradients into weight changes.

00:00:24.236 --> 00:00:29.542
Every fifty updates, the analysis program reads losses and gradients and writes a report.

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:34.431
At each decision, the agent reads those reports, and may rewrite the analysis.

00:00:34.851 --> 00:00:38.317
Or it rewrites the updater: new learning rates, a different rule per

00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:39.472
layer, a spike guard.

00:00:41.192 --> 00:00:44.075
The wrapper compares the agent's files with the running ones.

00:00:44.495 --> 00:00:47.846
A changed updater is built from the old one, keeping momentum.

00:00:48.266 --> 00:00:50.464
It runs on trial for twenty updates.

00:00:50.464 --> 00:00:53.291
A crash on its first update is undone exactly.

00:00:53.711 --> 00:00:56.874
A bad idea that does not crash waits for the next decision.

00:00:58.192 --> 00:01:01.349
A fixed recipe is decided up front and never changes.

00:01:02.365 --> 00:01:05.870
A reactive one reads its own probes and changes rules mid-run.

00:01:07.842 --> 00:01:10.320
Here a tenth of the labels are wrong.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.728
The plain recipe, in grey, memorizes them, and test loss climbs.

00:01:14.148 --> 00:01:17.952
The agent, in blue, sees dev loss rise, raises its learning rate,

00:01:17.952 --> 00:01:19.220
and averages its weights.

00:01:20.592 --> 00:01:24.022
Against the best recipe off the shelf, the margins are small in

00:01:24.022 --> 00:01:26.022
three language settings and clear in one.

00:01:28.092 --> 00:01:29.610
The agent is cheap.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:34.924
One image model run paid six dollars forty-two for it, beside seventy-four GPU hours.

00:01:36.142 --> 00:01:36.896
Remember this.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:40.290
A reactive optimizer repairs recipes that do not transfer.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.929
On a tuned recipe, expect a tie.

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:49.187
Two programs, a trial for every edit, and gains where nobody tuned a recipe.

00:01:49.607 --> 00:01:51.743
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:51.743 --> 00:01:52.353
I'm Lanyard.

00:01:52.353 --> 00:01:52.658
Bye!
